no concrete failure scenario, so it cannot gate; reported as major by the reviewer] HomeAssembly.stop() awaits scheduler.stop() before invoking coreLink.stop(). However, a running resend tick waits in Ingest.#sendDue() on link.send(), and the active socket write has neither cancellation nor a write deadline (ingest.ts:441,465 and socket-link.ts:77). Aborting the scheduler therefore does not release that wait. If outbound traffic is backpressured while inbound pings or messages continue, the liveness watchdog remains satisfied too. SIGTERM or a fatal-error restart can consequently remain blocked before the link is closed and before outbox/Ring cleanup runs. Initiate link cancellation or closure before awaiting scheduler work, ensure outstanding sends settle during shutdown, and cover stopping with a pending write.","finding_id":"finding-095da55dcd1393a6","lineage_id":"lin-ac630e740e7e3894","location":"bridge/src/host/home-assembly.ts:76","relevance":"current","resolution":"open","severity":"minor","source_local_id":"F001","title":"Unblock pending link writes before awaiting scheduler shutdown"}],"harness_id":"codex-cli-file-primary","run_id":"run-20261110-012921571-b48e7f6f","runtime_outcome":"completed","schema_version":"1.0","started_at":"2026-11-10T01:31:11.6245427+00:00","summary":"Completed risk-based inspection of the implemented frozen target, covering design and contract alignment, authentication and authorization, connector enrollment and transport, replay and freshness, persistence and secrets, leases, and host lifecycle. The controller's one declared governance command passed for the supplied digest. No tests or builds were run in this reviewer session. One major shutdown-ordering defect remains.","target_digest":"6ba2f53f7a91a8c9a05dd624e3908dcfac3905ea","termination_verified":true,"validation":"valid","verdict":"findings"}